## ── SESSION COMPARISON MODAL (feature: two sessions + monthly overlay) ──
# UI lives in index.html (#sessionCompareModal), styles in style.css (.ce-modal--compare,
# .compare-trend-card, .compare-month-insight, etc.), logic in App.js.
#
# Entry: header button #openSessionCompareBtn → openSessionCompareModal() →
# refreshCompareSessionOptions().
#
# DOM (authoritative):
#   #sessionCompareModal     — modal shell (.ce-modal--compare)
#   #compareSessionA         — Session 1 (baseline), options = completed sessions w/ analysis
#   #compareSessionB         — Session 2
#   #compareThisMonthBtn     — "This month · all sessions" (count in label when enabled)
#   #sessionCompareBody      — charts, banners, empty-state copy
#
# Data rules:
#   - Comparison charts need per-shot replay rows: results.replay.shots (same source as
#     ReportModal trend graphs). Confirmed shots use conf > 0.5 → getConfirmedTrendShotsFromResults().
#   - If both sessions lack replay shots, UI shows best-shot fallback text (no SVG charts).
#
# Two-session compare:
#   - getCompletedSessionsForCompare() — status completed + getSessionAnalysis(results), newest first
#   - refreshCompareSessionOptions() — if 0 completed: empty message; if 1: both dropdowns same +
#     "need at least two…"; if ≥2: options for both, default A = second-newest, B = newest (different IDs)
#   - renderSessionComparison(a,b) — blocks same id; four dual charts via buildDualLineCompareGraph:
#     speed (km/h), head_quality_score, symmetry_score, score — colors #06B6D4 vs #10B981
#   - sessionCompareDisplayLabel(session, peerSessions) — date string; if multiple sessions share a
#     calendar day, appends short time to disambiguate
#
# This month · all sessions:
#   - getCompletedSessionsThisMonth(state.sessionsCache) — created_at within current calendar month (local)
#   - updateCompareMonthButton() — disables button when < 2 month sessions; tooltip explains requirement
#   - renderMonthSessionsComparison() — banner + buildMonthPlayerInsightHtml() + buildMultiLineCompareGraph
#     for each metric (palette COMPARE_MULTI_COLORS, up to N distinct session lines)
#   - buildMonthPlayerInsightHtml — narrative "Your month at a glance" (momentum, bat speed, coaching
#     alerts, fatigue_detected, HEAD_LATERAL_DRIFT / STANCE_ASYMMETRIC-style flags across the month)
#   - "← Two-session compare" (data-compare-back) restores renderSessionComparison for current A/B picks
#
# When extending: keep SVG geometry aligned with ReportModal line-graph conventions; escapeHtml() on all
# dynamic labels and insight bullets.

